My main worry with using physical position is that I think it might smooth out the differences between my population and the reference genome and I want to be able to comment on the differences between the two with the use of this genetic map.
As you have mentioned in the tutorial, est.map() only re-estimates the map distance, if I order markers by physical position and then estimate the distance by est.map(), I think all the conflicts between the reference and my population will not be detected, isn't it?

And by using crossover counts you mean using "count xo" in method instead of "likelihood" right?

Thanks,

Prashant

